<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pompeii</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pompeii was an ancient town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campania">Campania</a>, southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-naples">Bay of Naples</a>, buried by the eruption of Mount Vesuvius in 79 CE. An <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oscan-language">Oscan</a> town later dominated by Samnites, it became a Roman colony in 80 BCE. Excavated since 1748, its preserved streets, houses, wall paintings and casts of the victims give an unrivalled picture of daily life in a Roman town, and it is a World Heritage Site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pompeii.jpg" alt="Pompeii" width="320" height="197" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carsten Steger · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aerial_image_of_Pompeii_and_Mount_Vesuvius_(view_from_the_southeast).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
